// ============================================================================
// xen-tool — ImGui launcher + stealth attach for Xen-supported games.
//
// User picks a game from the launcher, we shell-launch it (Steam URL when
// available), then poll for the process by exe name.  Once it's up we attach
// via the driver (SetPid only — we never open a handle against the target)
// and show a details panel: PID, process uptime, main module base/size, and
// a probe of commonly-loaded UE modules so the user can see what the target
// has actually mapped.
//
// Stealth envelope stays identical to xen-dumper:
//   - xen-tool is its own process with its own swapchain.
//   - Window is topmost + layered + click-through; DWM composites it over the
//     game at the OS level.  The game's render loop is never touched.
//   - All target-memory access exits usermode via IOCTL_READ_PROCESS_MEMORY /
//     IOCTL_GET_MODULE_BASE.  The driver walks CR3 in ring 0; the target sees
//     no handle, no thread, no allocation, no hook.
//
// For process discovery we use CreateToolhelp32Snapshot with TH32CS_SNAPPROCESS
// only (no SNAPMODULE — that would implicitly OpenProcess the target).  The
// process list snapshot queries kernel state, not the target itself.
// ============================================================================
